CONTRIBUTORS. Helen Edgar commits to this repository as well as Stimpunks, from
2026-09-26, and accepted this licence for what she contributes, and MIT for her
code. Her work here is hers and is credited to her in liner-notes.html; these
licences are how it travels. The exclusions below apply to what anybody brings,
her included.

Becky Hicks drew Bearmouse, Pandillo and Bunnybadger for stimpunks.org's About
page; they hang in chimera-obscura.html (the files are in art/). She is on the
Stimpunks board, and on 2026-10-18 she agreed that they travel under this
licence. They are hers and are credited to her in the room and in
liner-notes.html.

WHAT NEITHER LICENCE COVERS, and cannot:

  - The typefaces in fonts/. Each keeps its own licence and its own designer's
    copyright: most are under the SIL Open Font License and some under the
    Apache License 2.0. Which is which is read off each family's own record by
    tools/pull-foundry.py, kept in data/foundry-faces.json and shown on
    foundry.html; fonts/_sources.json says where each file came from. (This line
    said every face was OFL until 2026-09-28, which was never true.)
  - three.js, in vendor/, which draws Cel Street. It is the three.js authors'
    work under the MIT licence, which travels with it as vendor/three-LICENSE.txt.
  - The songs reachable from Pink Pony Club. Every one belongs to the artist who
    made it. None are hosted here; the jukebox links out and nothing more.
  - The borrowed names — Danny the Street, Pee-Wee's Playhouse, Pink Pony Club,
    Enid Sinclair, and McAnally's, Jim Butcher's pub in The Dresden Files.
    Homage is not licence. The short quotations of his books in A Quiet Pint
    stay his, under no onward licence from this site. See liner-notes.html.
  - Recordings in audio/ made by anybody other than us — a passage read aloud,
    a yell, anything with somebody's voice in it. The words may be ours; the
    voice is not, and it carries no onward licence. ("read by" was the wording
    here until the yell button needed recordings too, and a yell is not a
    reading.) Same reasoning as the photographs below: CC BY-SA cannot be
    revoked, and a person who lends us their voice has to be able to take it
    back. Ours, recorded by us, are covered by the licence above like any other
    thing we made.
  - The community photographs on Enid's polaroid wall. Every one stays the
    property of the people in it and the person who took it, used here with
    their permission and under no onward licence at all. This exclusion is
    load-bearing rather than tidy: CC BY-SA is irrevocable and permits
    commercial reuse, so a photograph published under it could not be taken
    back even after somebody withdrew consent. We promise a photo comes down
    when its subject says so, once, without a conversation. That promise is
    only true if the licence never applied to it. See polaroids.html.
  - The photographs in collection/, of our people's collections in The
    Collection Collection. Each belongs to the person who took it, used here
    with their permission and under no onward licence at all, for the polaroid
    wall's reason: a licence that cannot be revoked would make "it comes down
    when you say so" a promise the licence contradicted. The descriptions and
    captions written for them by the house are ours and are covered above.
  - Em's photographs of her press-on nails, and every row of nails cut from
    them in nails/ for the front page. Em makes and sells them as Ems Nails 4
    You (https://ems-nails4you.netlify.app/) and gave Stimpunks permission to
    use her photographs on Stimpunks.World however we like (2026-11-06).
    Permission to use is not a licence to pass on: they stay hers, under no
    onward licence from this site. The tool that cuts them is code and is
    covered by MIT above. See index.html and liner-notes.html.
  - Josephmooon's recordings and the words of "Up All Night" in The Small
    Hours. The recordings are streamed from the band's own site and hosted
    nowhere here. The lyrics are printed in full because Stimpunks holds
    permission to distribute the song and its lyrics, and permission to
    distribute is not permission to relicense: the words stay Ronan Boren's
    and the band's, under no onward licence from this site. See
    small-hours.html and liner-notes.html.

WHAT IS GIVEN AWAY MORE WIDELY:

  - The Broadsheet Broadside's sheets -- their words and their layout, wherever
    they appear, in broadsheet-broadside.html, in data/broadside.json and on
    paper -- are dedicated to the public domain under CC0 1.0, like the
    Stimpunks broadsides on stimpunks.org they are modelled on.
    https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/
    Print them, copy them, change them and hand them out with no permission and
    no credit required; each one asks for its credits to stay on it and cannot
    require it. The dedication covers only what is ours: the typefaces keep
    their own licences, and Danny the Street's name is DC Comics' on a sheet as
    anywhere else. The room around the sheets -- the ship, its copy, its
    stylesheet and its tools -- is covered by the licence above.

Relicensing something that is not ours would be exactly the failure this site
spends a whole page guarding against.
